 "web_search": true,
 "asked_at": "2026-10-18T00:45+08:00",
 "answer": "**Yes, you should strongly consider staying indoors and limiting outdoor activities in Kuala Lumpur today.** \n\nAir quality indexes (AQI) in parts of KL frequently register at levels that are considered **Unhealthy** or **Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups**, often driven by fine particulate matter ($PM_{2.5}$) and regional haze. \n\n### Why this matters for your asthma:\n* **Irritants and Inflammation:** $PM_{2.5}$ particles are microscopic enough to bypass your nose and upper airways, penetrating deep into your lungs. This causes airway inflammation, triggering asthma symptoms like coughing, wheezing, chest tightness, and shortness of breath.\n* **Increased Risk:** Individuals with asthma fall squarely into the sensitive group category. Elevated pollution levels can easily provoke an asthma flare-up or attack, even with minimal exertion.\n\n### Recommended Precautions:\n1. **Stay Indoors:** Keep windows and doors closed to prevent polluted air from entering your living space. If you have an air conditioner, run it on the recirculate/closed setting, and use a HEPA air purifier if available.\n2. **Postpone Outdoor Exercise:** Avoid jogging, walking, or any strenuous outdoor activities. Exercise forces you to breathe faster and deeper, pulling a higher volume of pollutants directly into your lungs.\n3. **Wear a Mask if You Must Go Out:** If stepping outside is unavoidable, wear a well-fitted particulate respirator mask (such as an N95 or KN95) rather than a standard cloth or surgical mask, as these offer better filtration against fine particles.\n4. **Keep Your Inhaler Close:** Always keep your quick-relief rescue inhaler (such as albuterol) with you at all times. Follow your prescribed asthma action plan closely.\n\n### When to Seek Medical Help:\nMonitor how you feel throughout the day. If you experience persistent coughing, wheezing, chest tightness, or if your rescue inhaler is not providing adequate relief, seek medical attention immediately.",
